The second file in this patch is `tools/check_reply_format.py` - a NEW file, a
standalone verifier for the reply rules the DELIVERY block now states. It is
deliberately a separate implementation, in the same shape as the per-routine
checkers already in tools/: the routine renders the reply, this verifies it,
and neither imports the other.

It is the same tool that lives in the outputs repo at
scripts/check_reply_format.py, trimmed to the reply case so it has no
dependency on the artifact bus.

  python3 tools/check_reply_format.py --reply /workspace/reply.txt

It exits 1 on any finding. Wire it into the routines that already save their
reply text (cron #23 saves /workspace/reply.txt; the others can do the same)
and run it before the reply is sent.

